Method

Simulated faults using ProxSim on FeFET and RRAM crossbars.

Evaluated on ResNet20, ResNet32, and NiN using CIFAR-10.

4-bit weights / 8-bit activations.

Tested multiple protection levels (2, 3, 4 bits) and PE batch configurations.

Key Results

From Table I and Fig. 3: 

Accuracy recovery:

Checksums recover >91–99% of baseline accuracy across models and technologies.

Often significantly outperform TMR, especially for FeFET.

Area & Latency Overhead:

Area: ~125–225% depending on bits protected (lower than TMR’s fixed 200%).

Latency: <40% (FeFET), <75% (RRAM).

Designers can trade off protection level vs. overhead.

Robustness:

Works for both FeFET and RRAM (technology-agnostic).

Corrects single-PE or single-column faults in real time; multi-fault cases trigger recomputation.
